# Publish changes to the live site

This repo is the Defenders volleyball site. GitHub Pages deploys from `main`. A local edit is not live until it is on `origin/main`.

After you finish a change the user asked for, commit it and push to `origin/main` in the same turn. Do not wait to be asked, and do not stop after a local edit.

- Commit only the files for that change. Leave secrets and credentials untracked.
- Push with a normal `git push` to `main`. Do not force-push.
- `git:https://github.com` is already stored, so set `GCM_INTERACTIVE=Never` and `GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0` and push without a login prompt.
- Tell the user the push finished and that Pages will update from it. A hard refresh shows the new `app.js` if the browser cached the old one.

Skip the push only when the user says to keep the change local, or when there is nothing to commit.
